"""Reports derive their numbers from retained results, including failed goals."""
from pathlib import Path
from pln_chess.common import ROOT,read_json,write_json
from evaluation.cycle3 import read_gzip

PACKAGES=[
 ('C5-01','complete','Four exact C4 baseline reruns, versioned snapshots and provenance lock','baseline.json'),
 ('C5-02','complete','Executable native capability matrix, including negative conjunction results','native-probes/audit.json'),
 ('C5-03','complete','Versioned typed premises, raw pre/post frames and disclosed host abstractions','model/C5-full.json'),
 ('C5-04','partial','Clean local combination holdout; exposure and temporal tests remain structural controls rather than fully independent factorial curricula','factorial.json.xz'),
 ('C5-05','complete','Strict proof planner and negative feasibility result; no defensible new positive legality theorem','proofs/before-after.json.xz'),
 ('C5-06','complete','Original 49 negative proofs retained; every newly resolved negative has family-removal evidence','proofs/new-negative-counterfactuals.json.xz'),
 ('C5-07','partial','Three temporal trust modes and scoped observations; no learned theorem of complete historical legality','temporal.json'),
 ('C5-08','partial','Causal activation/disabled/sham study executed; host-proposed descriptors, no native abstraction discovery or production gain','induction.json'),
 ('C5-09','complete','Source/ancestor exclusion, replay, rollback, corruption and family counterfactuals','proofs/family-counterfactuals.json.xz'),
 ('C5-10','complete','Whole candidate sets, new games, calibration and two representation ablations; positive research targets fail','comparison.json'),
 ('C5-11','partial','Shared typed calculations, exported DAG references and full cache parity; inherited C4 proof occurrences still repeat','benchmarks/C5.json'),
 ('C5-12','complete','Compatible schema dispatch, CLI modes and inspector proof gaps','ui-verification.json'),
 ('C5-13','complete','Tests and locked clean reproduction with explicit native failures','verification.json'),
 ('C5-14','complete','Versioned reports, exact changed-file list, manifest and local delivery','manifest.json')]

def pct(x):return 'undefined' if x is None else f'{100*x:.2f}%'

def report(out):
    out=Path(out);docs=ROOT/'docs/cycle5';docs.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
    comparison=read_json(out/'comparison.json');run=read_json(out/'run.json');ind=read_json(out/'induction.json');new=read_json(out/'new-negative-summary.json')
    rows=['| Model / split | Positions | Candidates | Supported legal | Supported illegal | Unknown | False legal / illegal | Precision | Recall | F1 | Exact sets |',
          '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for name,splits in comparison.items():
        for split,v in splits.items():
            m=v['metrics'];r=read_gzip(out/v['artifact'])
            rows.append(f"| {name} / {split} | {len(r['positions'])} | {m['candidates']} | {m['true_positive']} | {m['true_negative']} | {m['unknown']} | {m['false_positive']} / {m['false_illegal']} | {pct(m['precision'])} | {pct(m['recall'])} | {pct(m['f1'])} | {pct(m['exact_move_set_accuracy'])} |")
    table='\n'.join(rows)
    packages='| Package | Status | Actual outcome | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join(f'| {p} | {s} | {d} | [{e}](../../artifacts/cycle5/{e}) |' for p,s,d,e in PACKAGES)
    write_json(out/'package-status.json',[dict(package=p,status=s,outcome=d,evidence=e) for p,s,d,e in PACKAGES])
    (docs/'generalization-results.md').write_text('# Generalization results\n\n'+table+'\n\nC5 strict positive recall is zero and precision is undefined because no positive legality theorem is established. Zero false-legal observations therefore do not demonstrate useful positive prediction. Any exact empty move sets are terminal-position matches. C4 conditional local projections are a different claim and remain reported as the prior baseline.\n\nAll reports use the unchanged candidate grammar and include unknowns in recall. Every report includes in-board-only and per-family/per-piece/special-move metrics, raw TVs, model/dataset hashes, bootstrap intervals and incomplete counts. Boundary negatives do not establish chess competence. New games have 16 independent source games with two sampled positions each, plus four validation games. The full trajectories are retained.\n\nThe factorial-only model omits C4 observation hypotheses and retains only independently trained bridge conditionals. Fine and abstract combinations, declared structural families, symmetry and source ancestry are disjoint. Full C4 prior overlap is separately disclosed; it cannot be called novel transfer. Repeated synthetic training rows share dependence groups. Sample-efficiency results report the first success among measured prefixes, not a minimal-context theorem.\n\nCalibration uses only the new validation games. Confidence is not treated as probability. Risk curves only suppress already-admitted negative witnesses as display confidence increases; the detection floor remains 0.25. See [calibration](../../artifacts/cycle5/calibration.json), [risk curves](../../artifacts/cycle5/selective-risk.json), [factorial evidence](../../artifacts/cycle5/factorial.json.xz), and [dataset audit](../../artifacts/cycle5/datasets/dataset.json).\n')
    (docs/'induction-results.md').write_text(f"# Causal induction findings\n\n{len(ind['rules'])} candidate conditionals were induced from a population of {len(ind['population'])} original training groups. Native activation supports {ind['local_activations']} local control predictions; {ind['local_false_legal_if_misused']} would be false-legal if misused as global conclusions. Global classification changes: {ind['global_classification_changes']}.\n\nDisabled, enabled and sham controls share data and the 64-proposal cap. A consequent rule is absent before induction, but its typed candidate descriptor is proposed by bounded host search. This is not native invention of a relational abstraction. Sham rules retain identical ancestry and receive no extra revision confidence. Geometry-to-local activation cannot establish destination, obstruction, temporal or safety composition. Production induction remains disabled.\n\n[Population, measured marginals, native expressions, TVs, provenance and all control outcomes](../../artifacts/cycle5/induction.json).\n")
    perf=['# Matched performance\n','| Model / fixture | Candidates | Reference s / calls | Cold s / calls | Warm s / calls | Complete proof parity |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|'];memory=[]
    for name in ('C4','C5'):
        b=read_json(out/f'benchmarks/{name}.json')
        for r in b['corpus']:
            vals=[f"{r['runs'][x]['elapsed_seconds']:.3f} / {r['runs'][x]['native_invocations']}" for x in ('reference','cold','warm')]
            perf.append(f"| {name} / {r['fixture']} | {r['candidates']} | {' | '.join(vals)} | {r['full_proof_parity']} |")
        memory.append(f"\n{name} checkpoint: {b['checkpoint_bytes']:,} bytes; fresh-address-space peak: {b['peak_process_rss_kib']:,} KiB.\n")
    perf.extend(memory)
    perf.append(f"\nFull research parent peak: {run['research_parent_peak_rss_kib']:,} KiB. Native subprocess-tree peak is not aggregated. Corpus timings are single measurements per mode/position; evaluation reports contain p50/p95 over positions, not repeated-run uncertainty.\n\nC5 shares typed premise calculations within a position and exposes content-addressed DAG references. It still constructs the inherited C4 candidate proof occurrences. Cache scope includes runtime, model, ledger, position, policy, temporal receipt and suppressed families. Reference/cached comparisons require complete candidate, TV, classification, rule and evidence equality. Budgets count combined stages and estimated proof metadata; they are not OS memory caps. [Raw C5 benchmark](../../artifacts/cycle5/benchmarks/C5.json).\n")
    (docs/'performance.md').write_text('\n'.join(perf))
    (docs/'engineering-report.md').write_text(f"# Cycle 5 engineering report\n\nStarting reference `d5cfcb126acc9c3e5da669744d661e6895fb9303`. Build source `{run['source_head']}`. Final delivery is the local commit containing this report and its manifest; no push is authorized for this cycle.\n\nCycle 5 produces stricter, inspectable proof gaps and reusable native negative transfer. It does **not** complete positive compositional chess legality. All default positive claims abstain, so recall is zero and precision is undefined. This is a substantial coverage loss relative to C4's conditional local projection. Aspirational positive-recall and exact-set targets are not achieved.\n\nAll 49 historical false-legal cases retain supported-illegal proofs. Across the declared splits, {new['count']} additional C4 unknowns receive C5 negative proofs; decisive-family removal changes classification in {new['removal_changes_classification']} cases. Observed false-illegal among those changes: {new['false_illegal']}. Every new negative retains the complete native proof and removal result; alternative witnesses are not hidden.\n\n## Package matrix\n\n{packages}\n\n## Results and evidence\n\n{table}\n\nMachine-readable results include denominator, model version, dataset hash, confidence policy, per-piece and in-board metrics. [Generalization and overlap policy](generalization-results.md), [native boundary](composition-feasibility.md), [temporal semantics](temporal-semantics.md), [induction study](induction-results.md), [performance](performance.md), and [verification](verification.md) describe limitations. [All changed paths](../../artifacts/cycle5/changed-files.json) and the [artifact manifest](../../artifacts/cycle5/manifest.json) define the delivery.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```bash\nTMPDIR=/dev/shm bash scripts/cycle5_reproduce.sh\n.venv/bin/pln-chess composition-audit\n.venv/bin/pln-chess evaluate --checkpoint artifacts/cycle5/model/C5-full.json --split independent-games\n```\n\n## Ranked next questions\n\n1. Can a separately validated native operator establish a positive conjunction with explicit dependence semantics? Require a previously unseen positive combination and adverse controls before changing C5's default.\n2. Can a native safety theorem summarize independent opponent frames without treating absent threats as safety? Measure recovery of legal recall, not just zero false positives.\n3. Can independently sourced temporal premises establish special-move eligibility and survive truncation/conflict tests? Keep event consistency separate from legal history.\n4. Can induction propose a useful relation absent from host abstractions? Require enabled/disabled/sham classification differences on a fresh holdout.\n5. Can inherited C4 proof occurrences be interned while preserving bindings, lineage and complete proof parity? Measure fresh-process memory and total serialized proof cost.\n")
    return docs/'engineering-report.md'
